SUMMARY







.ti 3
This is the third revision of the UNIX BATCH operators guide
incorporating changes available under Level 6.5 of the
UNIX operating system.
.ti 3
It was written in the hope that it would not be like other manuals
on batch station operation.
We hoped to give you a manual which was informative and
readable as well as technical in a simple minded way.
.ti 3
The manual is divided into three basic sections each readable
alone or in combination with the others.
.ti 3
Chapter two is on hardware but in no way tells what to do when the
maintenance man is away.
.ti 3
Chapter three will give you some interesting insights into the
software both at the CYBER end as well as the batch station.
.ti 3
However chapter four is probably the most interesting from the
operations point of view.
This section has been extensively revised for the introduction of Level 6
UNIX and now contains
detailed information ranging from turning the
PDP-11 on, decriptions of all operational commands and turning the
PDP-11 off, to "what to do 'till the GURU arrives".
.ti 3
For quick reference extracts we would refer you to:

 	* Commands - Appendix C
	* Start up and close down - Appendix A
	* Error messages - Appendix E
	* Files and directories - Appendix F
	* Peripheral cleaning and maintenance - Appendix D
	* Local batch and local system changes - Appendix B
	* The GURUs to call for help - Appendix G

.ti 3
This is version three of the manual and is once again by no means perfect
(as you may find out).
For this reason we ask you to read it and tell us what we have done
wrong and what we should do to fix it (tell a GURU).




